<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Downs</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1639">1639</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the Downs was a naval battle fought on 21 October 1639 off the coast of Kent, during the Eighty Years' War. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> fleet under Lieutenant-Admiral <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maarten-tromp">Maarten Tromp</a> destroyed most of a large Spanish armada carrying troops to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>, which had sheltered in English waters. The victory ended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s attempts to reinforce the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/army-of-flanders">Army of Flanders</a> by sea and marked the passing of naval supremacy to the Dutch.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-downs.jpg" alt="Battle of the Downs" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Willem van de Velde the Younger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Battle_of_the_Downs_by_Willem_van_de_Velde.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
